                <pb facs="0062" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/2437: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-25T20:00:00-04:30">August 25, 1943—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 26—4:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>761. My 727, August 13, 8 p.m.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d49-f1"/> During a
                    conversation today with Foreign Minister Parra Perez, inquired his views
                    concerning the Colombian proposal for the formation of a bloc. The Minister
                    replied that he is now examining the Colombian proposal with [President] Medina
                    who only yesterday returned to his office from an inspection of the flooded
                    areas. The Minister expressed his own view that such matters should be dealt
                    with on a Pan-American basis rather than through blocs. This has been the tenor
                    of press editorial comment in recent days.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Bogotá.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
